WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:09.370
- [Narrator:] New York City. How do you shine

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:10.750
when there are eight million people

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:13.400
also striving for the spotlight?

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.660
How do you make it where others falter?

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:18.940
Is it luck, hard work, determination

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:20.950
that brings you the fame you seek?

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:24.860
Maybe all of the above.
But this isn't my story.

00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:26.090
It's Cole Anthony's.

00:00:26.090 --> 00:00:27.460
- [Public Address Announcer:] Cole Anthony!

00:00:29.713 --> 00:00:33.902
♪♪♪ I, I, I used to feel so devastated ♪♪♪
- [Announcer 1:] Oh, he puts it home with the right!

00:00:33.902 --> 00:00:35.044
Cole Anthony!

00:00:35.044 --> 00:00:36.210
♪♪♪ At the time, I thought we'd never make it ♪♪♪

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:37.838
- [Announcer 2:] Great pass. That was a dime.

00:00:37.838 --> 00:00:39.950
♪♪♪ But now, we on our way to greatness ♪♪♪

00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:41.050
- [Announcer 3:] The
highest-touted prospect.

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:42.439
- [Announcer 4:] No. 1 
guard in the country.

00:00:42.439 --> 00:00:44.578
♪♪♪ And all it ever took was patience ♪♪♪

00:00:44.578 --> 00:00:45.460
- [Announcer 5:] Another three!

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:48.123
- [Announcer 6:] Sensational in his North Carolina debut.

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:52.500
- [Commentator 1:] Cole Anthony is out with a knee injury...

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:53.333
- [Commentator 2:] He's
gonna be off the court

00:00:53.333 --> 00:00:56.500
for at least a month.
- ...and is out indefinitely.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:58.580
- [Greg Anthony:] No matter how bad things go,

00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:02.100
he has supreme confidence.
- [Commentator 3:] The most competitive player

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:04.637
this NBA draft.
- [Commentator 4:] He has high steal potential.

00:01:04.637 --> 00:01:05.960
- [Commentator 3:] And I
think that he's NBA-ready.

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.840
- [Commentator 5:] Can run a team right now.

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:09.353
- [Commentator 6:] And he can be dynamite.

00:01:10.727 --> 00:01:13.240
♪♪♪ At times, I thought we'd never make it ♪♪♪

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:14.905
- [Commentator 7:] Ideal size.

00:01:14.905 --> 00:01:19.072
♪♪♪ Now, we on our way to greatness ♪♪♪

00:01:22.707 --> 00:01:23.882
[Whistle blowing]
♪♪♪ Right here ♪♪♪

00:01:23.882 --> 00:01:26.520
♪♪♪ For the crown right here ♪♪♪

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:30.170
- [Narrator:] Basketball in New York
is a different animal, man.

00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:32.860
Basketball's in this city's
soul. It's on every corner

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:35.276
and in every park.
- [Public address announcer:] There we go.

00:01:35.276 --> 00:01:38.521
Make some noise!
[Crowd cheering]

00:01:38.521 --> 00:01:40.260
- [Narrator:] There've been
so many legendary players

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:41.853
that came from these streets.

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:45.810
It's a badge of honor to
be a baller from New York.

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:49.817
- [PA announcer:] Yeah, guard
me! Guard me! Guard me!

00:01:49.817 --> 00:01:51.420
'Scuse me.
[Crowd cheering]

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:54.710
- [Kenny Smith:] Playing basketball in
New York is kind of a, it's a way of life.

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:56.150
There's not a lot of
gyms in New York City,

00:01:56.150 --> 00:01:58.760
but there's a lot of basketball courts.

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:00.583
So everyone plays the game.

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:03.390
- [Franklyn Calle:] You know, you're born into it.

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:05.450
It's what you do. Regardless
of your background,

00:02:05.450 --> 00:02:08.017
where your parents come from, you hoop.

00:02:08.017 --> 00:02:10.817
- [PA announcer 1:] Move out
the way. Move out the way.

00:02:10.817 --> 00:02:12.403
[Crowd cheering]

00:02:12.403 --> 00:02:13.670
- [Smith:] There's eight million people there,

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:16.030
so how do you differentiate yourself

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:17.760
from eight million people?

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:19.870
You know, you have to
be special, and you have

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:22.517
to be loud in doing it, at times.

00:02:22.517 --> 00:02:24.327
[Crowd cheering]

00:02:24.327 --> 00:02:25.663
- [PA announcer 2:] I am the best.
- [Spectator 1:] I told you!

00:02:27.134 --> 00:02:28.226
- [Spectator 2:] Yessir.

00:02:28.226 --> 00:02:31.140
♪♪♪ And we goin' down in history ♪♪♪

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:34.420
- I think Cole Anthony
is New York basketball,

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:36.580
New York hoops. He is what you'd think

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:37.980
when you think of a New York player:

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:40.533
gritty, tough, assertive.

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:46.470
Grimy. He is New York basketball in that sense.

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:49.893
He is your typical New York City guard.

00:02:51.232 --> 00:02:53.982
[Crowd cheering]

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:56.730
- [Cole Anthony:] One redeeming quality all of us have

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:57.920
is that we're all tough.

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:00.570
I mean, you not gon' find
no guards from New York

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:03.790
that play dead and just let
someone walk all over them.

00:03:03.790 --> 00:03:06.820
They're gon' give it they
all, no matter who it is.

00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:09.060
- [Narrator:] A New York legend doesn't just appear.

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:12.650
Nah, a New York legend is
built. And for Cole Anthony,

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:15.580
his journey began before he came to be—

00:03:15.580 --> 00:03:20.580
as a son of NBA player and
New York Knick Greg Anthony.

00:03:20.672 --> 00:03:21.808
[Crowd cheering]
- [Announcer 1:] Greg Anthony

00:03:21.808 --> 00:03:23.299
with an open three.

00:03:23.299 --> 00:03:24.915
- [Announcer 2:] Anthony
penetrates to the bucket.

00:03:24.915 --> 00:03:27.340
[Crowd cheering]
- [Announcer 1:] Anthony to the reverse.

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:28.173
Yes!
- [Announcer 3:] Anthony's been one

00:03:28.173 --> 00:03:29.590
of the unsung heroes for the Knicks.

00:03:29.590 --> 00:03:30.438
[Celebratory music]
- [Announcer 1:] What a performance

00:03:30.438 --> 00:03:31.771
by Greg Anthony!

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:34.780
[Crowd cheering]

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:36.620
- [Cole Anthony:] It was always cool just to have that dad,

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:38.090
and it was not until I was older

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:40.380
that I really learned to appreciate, I mean, my dad

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:42.826
being a former NBA player,
being someone who had been

00:03:42.826 --> 00:03:44.170
through the process
that I wanna be through.

00:03:44.170 --> 00:03:49.170
- He was born in 2000, so
he never, ever saw me play.

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:52.440
You know, he obviously would know

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:55.370
because people would say
something about it, but for him,

00:03:55.370 --> 00:03:57.514
he just always played cuz he loved it.

00:03:57.514 --> 00:03:59.170
♪♪♪ I woke up this morning inspired ♪♪♪

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:01.410
- [Cole Anthony:] My mom has this picture of
me from, I think I was

00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:03.250
like six months old, it was,
like, before I could walk,

00:04:03.250 --> 00:04:05.110
just throwing a
basketball at the hoop.

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:07.030
I just always had that
dream when I was younger.

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:08.810
I mean, I wasn't even
thinking about how good I was.

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:11.153
I was just thinking that
I wanted to be in the NBA.

00:04:12.072 --> 00:04:14.170
♪♪♪ Don't let 'em take your soul away ♪♪♪
♪♪♪ Don't let 'em take your soul away, come on ♪♪♪

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:16.020
- [Greg Anthony:] Towards the end of the fifth grade,

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:20.090
you know, he was playing baseball,
and I'm a big baseball fan.

00:04:20.090 --> 00:04:22.860
And he came to me after the
game, and I'll never forget it.

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:25.950
He was like, "Dad, you know,
I just want to tell you,

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:27.170
I don't want to play baseball anymore.

00:04:27.170 --> 00:04:29.101
I just want to focus on basketball."

00:04:29.101 --> 00:04:32.693
And it caught me off guard,
quite frankly, cuz one, you know,

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:36.550
he wasn't that good at
basketball at the time.

00:04:36.550 --> 00:04:38.340
- [Cole Anthony:] I wasn't even aware that I was that bad.

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:40.670
But, I mean, my friends will tell
you I wasn't that good,

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:44.100
but, I mean, it's just, I always just
had love for the sport.

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:47.573
- [Greg Anthony:] He would compete like
crazy, but his skill set,

00:04:48.590 --> 00:04:51.910
I didn't envision him as
necessarily developing

00:04:51.910 --> 00:04:53.883
into what he's developing into.

00:04:56.033 --> 00:04:57.324
[Heavy, dramatic music]

00:04:57.324 --> 00:04:59.333
♪♪♪ I won't back down ♪♪♪

00:04:59.333 --> 00:05:03.936
♪♪♪ I was born to win ♪♪♪
♪♪♪ Step by step ♪♪♪

00:05:03.936 --> 00:05:06.781
♪♪♪ I won't back down ♪♪♪

00:05:06.781 --> 00:05:10.080
♪♪♪ I was born to win ♪♪♪
♪♪♪ Step by step ♪♪♪

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:11.830
- [Cole Anthony:] I was just focused on being the best

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:13.720
individual player I can
be. I wasn't really worried

00:05:13.720 --> 00:05:16.420
about following footsteps
of anyone, not even my dad.

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:17.750
I just. My own person.

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:20.080
I wanna do everything I can for myself.

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:22.698
♪♪♪ I was born to win ♪♪♪
♪♪♪ I refuse to lose ♪♪♪

00:05:22.698 --> 00:05:24.436
♪♪♪ I refuse to break ♪♪♪

00:05:24.436 --> 00:05:25.818
♪♪♪ Pushin' for the win ♪♪♪

00:05:25.818 --> 00:05:27.600
♪♪♪ No matter what it takes ♪♪♪

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:29.454
♪♪♪ I refuse to lose ♪♪♪

00:05:29.454 --> 00:05:30.287
♪♪♪ I refuse to break ♪♪♪

00:05:30.287 --> 00:05:32.060
- His body started to grow a little bit.

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:33.720
He started to get a little more athletic.

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:35.730
Skill set was starting to develop.

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:39.250
The better he got, the
better he wanted to get.

00:05:39.250 --> 00:05:42.280
So, when he started to get
some national recognition,

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:45.130
it kind of fueled his fire,
and it made him work harder.

00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:47.230
- [Announcer 1:] Oh, my, what
a block by Cole Anthony.

00:05:47.230 --> 00:05:49.370
- [Announcer 2:] Anthony's got it.
- [Announcer 3:] Oh! Gets it down.

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:51.920
What a play.
- He would always want

00:05:51.920 --> 00:05:55.111
to do things better than I
did them at certain stages.

00:05:55.111 --> 00:05:58.770
Cuz he's, you know, like, "Dad when's
the first time you dunked?"

00:05:58.770 --> 00:06:01.050
And I said, "Well, the ninth
grade, you know, was the first time."

00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:04.112
He says, "Well, you know, I wanna be able
to dunk in the eighth grade."

00:06:04.112 --> 00:06:06.640
♪♪♪ I was born to win ♪♪♪
♪♪♪ Step by step ♪♪♪

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:08.250
- I think I've become my own player.

00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:09.740
I don't think I lean on
my dad's name anymore.

00:06:09.740 --> 00:06:11.334
I think I've created my own name.

00:06:11.334 --> 00:06:12.167
♪♪♪ I was born to win ♪♪♪

00:06:12.167 --> 00:06:14.170
♪♪♪ Step by step ♪♪♪
- [Narrator:] It's hard

00:06:14.170 --> 00:06:16.980
to come up in this city, but once you do,

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:19.433
damn, the light shines bright.

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:21.970
Cole went to Archbishop Molloy,

00:06:21.970 --> 00:06:24.270
where some of the most
legendary New York players

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:28.537
balled in high school. 
And the hype just exploded.

00:06:28.537 --> 00:06:31.810
♪♪♪ I was born to win ♪♪♪
♪♪♪ Step by step ♪♪♪

00:06:31.810 --> 00:06:36.040
- [Calle:] The fall of 2015, you know,
rumblings around the city.

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:37.640
You know, people start to talk.

00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:40.430
There's this freshman
out in Archbishop Molloy

00:06:40.430 --> 00:06:42.910
that as a freshman is
starting on the varsity squad.

00:06:42.910 --> 00:06:45.760
So first and foremost, in
New York City, the CHSAA,

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:47.340
which is the Catholic league, takes pride

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:49.540
in being one of the toughest
leagues in the country.

00:06:49.540 --> 00:06:52.170
You don't play as a freshman
on varsity squad, period.

00:06:52.170 --> 00:06:53.890
Very, very rare. It doesn't happen.

00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:56.470
Molloy's had, you know,
they've had Kenny Smith, you know,

00:06:56.470 --> 00:06:59.250
Kenny Anderson and Russ Smith.
They've had some guards come out

00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:01.610
of there, but no one has
been able to come in

00:07:01.610 --> 00:07:03.850
right off the bat and
just start, day one.

00:07:03.850 --> 00:07:05.770
- [Announcer:] Cole Anthony, what a finish.

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:07.450
Cole Anthony, he gets it.

00:07:07.450 --> 00:07:09.550
- [Calle:] So by the time junior year comes around,

00:07:09.550 --> 00:07:10.610
Cole worked his way all the way up

00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:12.980
to be No. 1 point
guard in the country.

00:07:12.980 --> 00:07:15.350
That's essentially how we
came upon deciding, you know, it was time

00:07:15.350 --> 00:07:17.010
for Cole to be on the SLAM cover.

00:07:17.010 --> 00:07:18.590
- [Photographer:] Cole, look at me.

00:07:18.590 --> 00:07:19.720
There you go.

00:07:19.720 --> 00:07:21.780
- [Calle:] We were trying to figure
out when was the last time

00:07:21.780 --> 00:07:25.490
that the No. 1 point guard
in the country was based

00:07:25.490 --> 00:07:26.660
in New York, in New York City.

00:07:26.660 --> 00:07:28.980
And we said, "Oh, shoot, the
last time that happened was,

00:07:28.980 --> 00:07:33.980
like, 20-plus years ago. It
was Stephon Marbury, 1995."

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:36.316
So, it became this historic thing.

00:07:36.316 --> 00:07:37.518
♪♪♪ Beatin' down ya block ♪♪♪

00:07:37.518 --> 00:07:38.999
♪♪♪ Bangin' through ya 16s ♪♪♪

00:07:38.999 --> 00:07:40.324
♪♪♪ Go on, walk it out ♪♪♪

00:07:40.324 --> 00:07:41.857
♪♪♪ Girl, you know what I mean ♪♪♪

00:07:41.857 --> 00:07:43.262
♪♪♪ I'm on fire, I'm on fire ♪♪♪

00:07:43.262 --> 00:07:44.095
♪♪♪ I'm on fire ♪♪♪

00:07:44.095 --> 00:07:44.928
I remember, on the cover,

00:07:44.928 --> 00:07:45.980
we put, like, "Prince of New York"
or something like that.

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:48.050
And then like two months
later, he leaves New York

00:07:48.050 --> 00:07:50.650
to go to Virginia to finish
his high school career.

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:52.790
And, you know, a lot of people were like, 
you know: "Why,

00:07:52.790 --> 00:07:55.527
why is he leaving? Why isn't he staying?"

00:07:56.505 --> 00:07:59.540
♪♪♪ I been having this vision ♪♪♪

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:01.820
- [Narrator:] Cole swapping fame
and status in New York

00:08:01.820 --> 00:08:05.430
for Oak Hill definitely caught
a lot of people off guard.

00:08:05.430 --> 00:08:07.890
Cuz, see, New York
isn't used to being shunned,

00:08:07.890 --> 00:08:09.560
but they couldn't see his vision was set

00:08:09.560 --> 00:08:10.880
on something greater.

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:12.360
♪♪♪ And I gotta do what I gotta do ♪♪♪

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:14.906
♪♪♪ Mask on my face. Black in my veins ♪♪♪

00:08:14.906 --> 00:08:16.400
♪♪♪ I gotta do what I gotta do ♪♪♪

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:18.270
- [Cole Anthony:] The reason I did that
was just cuz I felt

00:08:18.270 --> 00:08:21.110
like, it's just there wasn't much left for me

00:08:21.110 --> 00:08:22.890
in New York, just in terms of basketball.

00:08:22.890 --> 00:08:25.670
I felt that I wanted to play
in a more competitive league,

00:08:25.670 --> 00:08:30.010
play with dudes that were
better. And so we felt that going

00:08:30.010 --> 00:08:31.882
to Oak Hill was the best choice.

00:08:31.882 --> 00:08:33.802
♪♪♪ Everything I was taught ♪♪♪
♪♪♪ I'mma break through it ♪♪♪

00:08:33.802 --> 00:08:36.410
- [Greg Anthony:] Cole just needed some maturity.

00:08:36.410 --> 00:08:38.940
He had never been to Oak Hill
until we dropped him off,

00:08:38.940 --> 00:08:41.850
and I remember he told me, you know, "Dad,

00:08:41.850 --> 00:08:44.610
whatever you say, I'm gonna trust you."

00:08:44.610 --> 00:08:46.080
- [Announcer 1:] That's a
beauty from Cole Anthony.

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:48.544
- [Announcer 2:] Oh, he puts it home with the right!

00:08:48.544 --> 00:08:50.280
Cole Anthony.

00:08:50.280 --> 00:08:52.224
- [Announcer 3:] No. 1 guard in the country.

00:08:52.224 --> 00:08:54.850
- It was a challenge for him,
especially how he had grown

00:08:54.850 --> 00:08:56.190
up the way he had grown up,

00:08:56.190 --> 00:09:00.880
but it did really help him
mature and become a man.

00:09:00.880 --> 00:09:02.230
- [Announcer:] Anthony getting past his

00:09:02.230 --> 00:09:04.450
man. Anthony with a windmill slam.

00:09:04.450 --> 00:09:05.790
Showcasing the flight.

00:09:05.790 --> 00:09:07.700
Blocked away by Anthony.

00:09:07.700 --> 00:09:09.790
The lob for Anthony is right there!

00:09:09.790 --> 00:09:10.893
[Crowd cheering]
♪♪♪ Light 'em up, light 'em up ♪♪♪

00:09:10.893 --> 00:09:13.310
♪♪♪ Light 'em up ♪♪♪

00:09:14.170 --> 00:09:15.530
- [Calle:] I think that that's part
of his story as well, right?

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:19.400
It's that, you know, he becomes the
top dog here in New York,

00:09:19.400 --> 00:09:21.267
then by senior year, he
makes a decision of, like,

00:09:21.267 --> 00:09:22.780
"I have to do what's best for me."

00:09:22.780 --> 00:09:25.560
And maybe a lot of people
in New York didn't, you know, felt some type

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:27.400
of way that he left, et cetera.

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:29.890
But that was definitely
what was best for him.

00:09:29.890 --> 00:09:33.170
- [Narrator:] Oak Hill is iconic, and
with Cole at the helm,

00:09:33.170 --> 00:09:35.990
scouts from all over
clamored to get a glimpse,

00:09:35.990 --> 00:09:38.460
and the offers rolled in.

00:09:38.460 --> 00:09:41.520
For him, the choice was obvious.

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:44.320
He knew it had to be somewhere legendary.

00:09:44.320 --> 00:09:46.780
- [Cole Anthony:] I really wanna thank all
the schools that recruited me.

00:09:46.780 --> 00:09:49.900
I mean, I had my final four,
but at the end of the day,

00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:51.480
we end up going with North Carolina.

00:09:51.480 --> 00:09:53.219
- [Offscreen:] Ooh.
- [TV Host:] North Carolina.

00:09:53.219 --> 00:09:56.290
[Talking and laughing over each other]

00:09:56.290 --> 00:09:58.520
- [Narrator:] Cole seemed
destined for greatness,

00:09:58.520 --> 00:10:00.410
but he had no idea the next step

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:02.910
would be the most challenging
chapter of his life.

